75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://www.mexicolore.co.uk/images-c/efa_70_2.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I do so love when an art team does their homework.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-30T05:23:42-08:00","id":1426688,"title":"","content":"Wow! This is a great show.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-06T03:39:45-08:00","id":1427443,"title":"","content":"We have <i>twins</i>!!! I love them and the way the model themselves after the Maya Hero Twins. I also think the show does logical conjecture from myth rather than outright invention really well. Did the Hero Twins have a special ball? No. Would a ball passed down from the Hero Twins be special? Sure! Is the gods taking possession of human bodies an attested belief? No. Does it make sense in the context of the gods needing human life and blood to do just about anything? Absolutely! Take note, storytellers out there, this is how it's done!<br /> It also continues to be obvious how much research went into this show. The cities we've seen so far are based on real-life places and include recognisable architectural features. This makes the show a great way to familiarise oneself with the world view and aesthetic of pre-Columbian Mesoamerica. My recommendation of this for Scion inspiration remains <i>strong</i>.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-06T08:29:45-08:00","id":1427460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sacerdos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1425547-onyx-equinox-and-mythological-fiction?p=1427443#post1427443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We have <i>twins</i>!!! I love them and the way the model themselves after the Maya Hero Twins. I also think the show does logical conjecture from myth rather than outright invention really well. Did the Hero Twins have a special ball? No. Would a ball passed down from the Hero Twins be special? Sure! Is the gods taking possession of human bodies an attested belief? No. Does it make sense in the context of the gods needing human life and blood to do just about anything? Absolutely! Take note, storytellers out there, this is how it's done!</div> </div> </div> </div>Are the weird, many-eyed monsters from the recent episode a thing in Mesoamerican myths? Or are they just a thing created for the show in the style of the myths, like the ball?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25753-a2a3a2a3","name":"a2a3a2a3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25753_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-06T11:34:08-08:00","id":1427473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>a2a3a2a3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1425547-onyx-equinox-and-mythological-fiction?p=1427460#post1427460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the weird, many-eyed monsters from the recent episode a thing in Mesoamerican myths? Or are they just a thing created for the show in the style of the myths, like the ball?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd actually been wondering about that myself. I listened to their podcast a bit, and it seems the monsters are, by and large, invented, mostly by taking native fauna (in this case, apparently, a coati of all things) and twisting it into something evil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}